# Spec-first + .cursor notes

Before diving into implementation, work with Doug to generate a TDD inspired spec within the `.cursor` directory.

Utilise the `.cursor` directory to manage notes and codebase specific learnings. This directory should always be gitignored.

Be proactive in restructuring the `.cursor` directory in ways that help you look things up better.

Always make use of your notes to understand how to work within the repository. Think of the `.cursor` directory as an extension of your brain - effectively your working memory. Key decisions, patterns, techniques and learnings should be tracked there. Clean up outdated information to avoid brainfog, and make sure it stays up-to-date.

Use regular conventional commits, rather than committing massive batches of change.

When putting comments in code, the comments should be accurate, but they should also focus on the "why" rather than the "what". Avoid overly verbose or obvious comments.
